<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Joanna II of Naples</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1373–1435</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Joanna II (1373–1435) was queen of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> from 1414 to 1435, succeeding her brother Ladislaus as the last ruler of the Angevin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durres">Durazzo</a> line. Her reign was dominated by favourites and shifting alliances, and she adopted in turn Alfonso V of Aragon and Louis III of Anjou as heirs. Her death without children opened a war of succession between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rene-of-anjou">René of Anjou</a> and Alfonso V.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/joanna-ii-of-naples.jpg" alt="Joanna II of Naples" width="320" height="441" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Franciscus3008 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Giovanna_II.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
